#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# appell_f3

#% text
# `appell_f3(a1, a2, b1, b2, c, x, y)` gives the Appell hypergeometric function `F3` of two variables.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `F3 = sum (a1)_m (a2)_n (b1)_m (b2)_n/((c)_(m+n) m! n!) x^m y^n` for `|x| < 1`, `|y| < 1` (DLMF 16.13.3).

#% item
# Numerical values: the sum over the rows of one variable of Gauss functions `hypergeometric_2f1` in the other (DLMF 16.13 summed over one index), the variable of smaller modulus outside; the inner Gauss function continues beyond the unit disk. Values are given when `|x| < 1` or `|y| < 1`.

#% item
# At `x = 0` or `y = 0` the function is a Gauss function.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
appell_f3(3, 2, 1, 2, 3, 1/3, 0.2)
#% output
#= 1.9529252485471225

#% cell
appell_f3(-2, -1, -2, 5, 2/3 + im, 0.4, 0.3)
#% output
#= 1.0258922705014568 + 0.8888650591954378im

#% cell
n(appell_f3(3, 2, 1, 2, 3, 1/3, 2/5), 20)
#% output
#= 2.725409214504086580700

#% cell
appell_f3(im, 1, 1 + im, 3.2, 1/2, 0.5, 0.2 + 0.5*im)
#% output
#= -3.631531726069829 - 0.7603723741365631im

#% cell
appell_f3(a1, a2, b1, b2, c, 0, y)
#% output
#= hypergeometric_2f1(a2, b2, c, y)

